$ Seeded-fault fixture for tools/validate.py - every check should fire once.
$ LENGTH MM
$ MASS TONNE
$ TIME S
$ FORCE N
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = FAULTS FIXTURE
SUBCASE 1
  LOAD = 10
  SPC = 1
SUBCASE 2
  LOAD = 99
  SPC = 1
BEGIN BULK
PARAM   POST    -1
$ ---- plate A: small field, mm-t-s steel
GRID    1               0.      0.      0.
GRID    2               1.      0.      0.
GRID    3               2.      0.      0.
GRID    4               0.      1.      0.
GRID    5               1.      1.      0.
GRID    6               2.      1.      0.
GRID    7               0.      2.      0.
GRID    8               1.      2.      0.
GRID    9               2.      2.      0.
$ duplicate grid id
GRID    5               1.      1.      0.
CQUAD4  1       1       1       2       5       4
CQUAD4  2       1       2       3       6       5
CQUAD4  3       1       4       5       8       7
CQUAD4  4       1       5       6       9       8
$ missing property
CQUAD4  99      77      2       3       6       5
PSHELL  1       1       1.      1
MAT1    1       210000.         .3      7.85-9
$ SPC set 1 in free field; grid 7 is also RBE2-dependent (conflict)
SPC1,1,123456,1,4,7
RBE2    300     8       123456  7
$ lumped mass on a grid nothing else uses, and an unused grid
GRID    500             5.      5.      5.
CONM2   400     500             .001
GRID    600             9.      9.      9.
$ cylindrical system for the load direction
CORD2C  5               0.      0.      0.      0.      0.      1.      +
+       1.      0.      0.
FORCE   20      109     5       10.     1.      0.      0.
LOAD    10      1.      2.      20
INCLUDE 'faults_mesh.inc'
ENDDATA
